Qwen3.8-Flash-Next decode patch 05: decode-time MoE block.

vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py

For up to 4 tokens, Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock computes the router and the
shared-expert gate in one GEMV whose last CTA also does top-k, renormalization
and the Marlin block alignment; runs the shared expert's INT6 gate/up (with
SiluAndMul) and down (with the final routed + gated-shared combine) as two
Triton kernels on the weights re-laid out once at load time into two bit
planes (same memory); and calls vLLM's own Marlin MoE GEMMs for the routed
experts. Prefill keeps FusedMoE; the shared expert then uses a Triton W6A16
GEMM on the planes. Only enabled for the configuration it was written for
(single-GPU MoE layout, INT4 Marlin experts, softmax + renormalize, no LoRA /
EPLB); anything else falls back to the original forward.

Set VLLM_MOE_FUSED_DECODE=0 to restore the original path (including Humming
for the shared expert).

